WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.756 --> 00:00:13.476
I’d like to dedicate this talk
to my three children:

00:00:14.156 --> 00:00:16.476
Phi, Mack

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.996
and Ella Roberta.

00:00:19.396 --> 00:00:20.956
(Inhales)

00:00:25.316 --> 00:00:28.516
If I stop breathing for two minutes,

00:00:28.556 --> 00:00:29.756
I would die.

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:34.836
It is the simplest thing
that all of us do unconsciously

00:00:34.876 --> 00:00:37.596
about 20,000 times a day.

00:00:37.596 --> 00:00:39.396
So normal

00:00:39.436 --> 00:00:42.956
that we forget that breathing
is the essence of life.

00:00:43.836 --> 00:00:46.796
My daughter, Ella Roberta,

00:00:46.836 --> 00:00:49.276
stopped breathing frequently

00:00:49.276 --> 00:00:55.156
and was resuscitated
numerous times by me at home

00:00:55.156 --> 00:00:58.676
and in hospital by her doctors,

00:00:58.716 --> 00:01:03.036
until suddenly, on the 15th of February,

00:01:03.076 --> 00:01:06.476
three weeks after her ninth birthday,

00:01:06.476 --> 00:01:09.076
she took her final breath.

00:01:09.956 --> 00:01:15.276
Ella was a healthy, clever,
sporty and funny girl.

00:01:15.876 --> 00:01:18.716
She had a lot of musical ability.

00:01:18.716 --> 00:01:20.516
At the time of her passing,

00:01:20.556 --> 00:01:23.436
she already played a dozen instruments.

00:01:23.756 --> 00:01:26.556
She was exceptionally good at football,

00:01:26.596 --> 00:01:30.476
cycling, skating, swimming and dancing.

00:01:31.076 --> 00:01:33.476
Ella was a great writer,

00:01:33.516 --> 00:01:36.356
and she was also pretty good at art.

00:01:36.916 --> 00:01:38.756
At the time of her passing,

00:01:38.796 --> 00:01:42.396
she had a reading age of 15 years.

00:01:43.796 --> 00:01:45.516
When she was six,

00:01:45.516 --> 00:01:51.316
the simple act of breathing
became the biggest challenge of her life.

00:01:51.636 --> 00:01:57.676
I rushed Ella to hospital
28 times in 28 months

00:01:57.676 --> 00:02:02.876
when she suddenly began suffering
severe respiratory issues.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:06.716
She was diagnosed
with life-threatening asthma

00:02:06.756 --> 00:02:08.716
at the age of seven.

00:02:08.756 --> 00:02:13.036
She was admitted
into intensive care five times

00:02:13.076 --> 00:02:17.236
and put in an induced coma
to save her life

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.796
when her lungs gave up on her.

00:02:20.556 --> 00:02:23.796
It wasn't until after
the first coroner's inquest

00:02:23.836 --> 00:02:26.156
in September 2014

00:02:26.196 --> 00:02:30.636
that I learned that her possible trigger
of her sudden illness

00:02:30.676 --> 00:02:34.316
was to do with "something in the air."

00:02:34.356 --> 00:02:37.116
But at that time,
we did not know what it was.

00:02:37.796 --> 00:02:42.036
Ella had one of the worst
cases ever of asthma

00:02:42.076 --> 00:02:44.556
recorded in the United Kingdom,

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:49.116
according to the pathologist
who carried out her postmortem.

00:02:49.956 --> 00:02:55.076
We as a family, we live 25 meters
from the South Circular

00:02:55.116 --> 00:02:56.756
in southeast London.

00:02:56.796 --> 00:02:59.436
It is one of the busiest roads in the UK.

00:02:59.476 --> 00:03:03.236
I later learned that air
pollution around our home

00:03:03.276 --> 00:03:08.476
was persistently far above the levels
deemed acceptable by the WHO.

00:03:08.836 --> 00:03:11.436
On every walk to school, every bike ride,

00:03:11.476 --> 00:03:14.276
every time Ella went outside,

00:03:14.276 --> 00:03:17.876
her body was absorbing
invisible, toxic air

00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:20.956
spewed out by petrol and diesel vehicles.

00:03:20.996 --> 00:03:26.036
A second inquest into Ella’s death,
just in December 2020,

00:03:26.076 --> 00:03:27.876
the coroner, Philip Barlow,

00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:33.916
he concluded that it was the excessive
illegal levels of air pollution,

00:03:33.956 --> 00:03:36.716
not only inducted her asthma,

00:03:36.756 --> 00:03:41.116
but it was the highest ever
on the night she died.

00:03:42.516 --> 00:03:44.196
As a result of this,

00:03:44.236 --> 00:03:47.276
Ella is the first person in the world

00:03:47.276 --> 00:03:51.676
to have air pollution
listed as a cause of death

00:03:51.716 --> 00:03:53.516
on her death certificate.

00:03:53.836 --> 00:03:56.916
Ella's story is unique, I admit,

00:03:56.956 --> 00:04:01.316
but her experience is shockingly ordinary.

00:04:01.996 --> 00:04:04.716
In too many countries around the world,

00:04:04.756 --> 00:04:06.716
air pollution exceeds

00:04:06.756 --> 00:04:10.996
what the WHO tells us
is acceptable to breathe.

00:04:11.516 --> 00:04:15.796
Fossil fuels, everyone,
they're killing us.

00:04:16.676 --> 00:04:19.196
Almost one in five premature deaths

00:04:19.196 --> 00:04:21.196
are linked to air pollution

00:04:21.236 --> 00:04:24.396
from combustion engines,
coal power plants,

00:04:24.436 --> 00:04:28.436
wood burning, ammonia, cooking stoves

00:04:28.436 --> 00:04:30.116
and other fossil fuels.

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:37.516
That is 8.7 million people a year
dying from heart attacks, cancer, strokes,

00:04:37.556 --> 00:04:43.276
dementia, suicide, depression,
stillbirths and miscarriages.

00:04:43.276 --> 00:04:44.916
And that's just the start.

00:04:45.796 --> 00:04:51.396
Children are the worst affected
due to their lungs still developing.

00:04:52.436 --> 00:04:56.436
Air pollution stunts the development
of lungs and brains.

00:04:56.436 --> 00:05:00.916
Scientists, believe it,
are finding soot in mothers placentas,

00:05:00.956 --> 00:05:06.756
meaning unborn babies
are directly exposed to the black carbon

00:05:06.796 --> 00:05:09.436
produced by motor traffic
and fuel burning.

00:05:09.836 --> 00:05:13.516
Like Ella, 93 percent of children
around the world

00:05:13.516 --> 00:05:15.476
are breathing unsafe air.

00:05:15.476 --> 00:05:20.636
The real tragedy of this is we know
how to solve this public health crisis.

00:05:20.676 --> 00:05:25.116
We need to shift from toxic fossil fuels

00:05:25.156 --> 00:05:29.596
to clean, electrified public
and active transport.

00:05:29.636 --> 00:05:34.436
The second inquest into Ella’s death
made it abundantly clear:

00:05:35.236 --> 00:05:38.356
Ella would still be here alive today

00:05:38.396 --> 00:05:41.196
if air pollution around our home

00:05:41.196 --> 00:05:44.396
had been within the WHO acceptable limits.

00:05:44.996 --> 00:05:50.276
Air pollution is an invisible
global pandemic.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.156
It's a silent killer.

00:05:52.676 --> 00:05:55.636
You know what,
unless you clean up the air,

00:05:55.636 --> 00:05:59.076
you will never resolve climate change.

00:05:59.076 --> 00:06:00.276
Do you know why?

00:06:00.276 --> 00:06:02.116
It's linked to global warming,

00:06:02.116 --> 00:06:03.876
acid rain,

00:06:03.916 --> 00:06:05.836
effects on wildlife,

00:06:05.836 --> 00:06:08.436
depletion of the ozone layer.

00:06:08.916 --> 00:06:11.436
But for me, this is personal.

00:06:11.836 --> 00:06:15.036
Eight years after Ella's death,

00:06:15.036 --> 00:06:18.556
I still visit respiratory doctors
with Ella’s siblings,

00:06:18.556 --> 00:06:22.116
who continue to be impacted
by excessive air pollution.

00:06:22.436 --> 00:06:27.436
As my children and I share a genetic link,

00:06:27.436 --> 00:06:31.636
we are equally susceptible
to air pollution.

00:06:32.636 --> 00:06:36.196
The WHO recently
strengthened its guidelines,

00:06:36.196 --> 00:06:42.116
and the evidence shows us
there is no such thing as safe levels.

00:06:43.156 --> 00:06:45.396
Every country in the world

00:06:45.396 --> 00:06:50.516
must enshrine these new
WHO guidelines into law now.

00:06:50.556 --> 00:06:52.076
I'm putting them on notice.

00:06:52.116 --> 00:06:57.756
(Applause)

00:06:57.796 --> 00:06:58.956
What do I want?

00:06:58.956 --> 00:07:00.636
I'll tell you what I want.

00:07:00.676 --> 00:07:04.036
I want every government
to guarantee their children

00:07:04.036 --> 00:07:07.716
the chance to live full and healthy lives.

00:07:08.036 --> 00:07:10.876
To be able to fully and safely breathe.

00:07:11.436 --> 00:07:16.916
Breathing clean air
is every child's human right.

00:07:17.396 --> 00:07:22.316
Governments have a duty of care
to protect their citizens.

00:07:22.636 --> 00:07:29.596
Remember, 350 million people
in the world have asthma,

00:07:29.596 --> 00:07:31.956
including me.

00:07:32.956 --> 00:07:35.876
(Breathing through inhaler)

00:07:42.156 --> 00:07:47.596
The fight to breathe clean air is real.

00:07:48.996 --> 00:07:52.956
When I say "Breathe life,"

00:07:52.956 --> 00:07:54.356
what do you say?

00:07:55.276 --> 00:07:57.716
You say, "Clean air is our right!"

00:07:57.756 --> 00:07:59.036
Breathe life!

00:07:59.076 --> 00:08:01.396
Audience: Clean air is our right!

00:08:01.956 --> 00:08:03.436
RAKD: Thank you for listening.

00:08:03.476 --> 00:08:04.716
Thank you very much.

00:08:04.716 --> 00:08:07.596
(Applause and cheers)

00:08:07.636 --> 00:08:10.636
[Take action on climate change
at countdown.ted.com]

